lifeos-nix patch f-derived-watch-config — default-on [derived_watch] in PULSE.toml

PROBLEM
  The DerivedWatch module (f-derived-watch-wire) is gated on config.derived_watch.enabled.
  Without a base config entry the gate is undefined; it defaults on via `!== false`, but the
  module deserves an explicit, documented base default so the behavior is visible in the
  shipped PULSE.toml rather than implicit.

FIX
  Add a [derived_watch] section to the base PULSE.toml, enabled = true (core sync default,
  per the "default-on for core sync services" direction). One hunk, config only.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  Base PULSE.toml only. User tier may override via PULSE.user.toml. Disjoint from f4-c
  (which flips egress modules off) and from the wire/module changes.

VERIFICATION
  Post-build PULSE.toml contains [derived_watch] enabled = true. Hunk via `diff -u`.

--- a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/PULSE.toml
+++ b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/PULSE.toml
@@ -56,6 +56,12 @@
 [performance]
 enabled = true

+[derived_watch]
+enabled = true
+# Event-driven regen of derived artifacts (PRINCIPAL_TELOS/LIFEOS_STATE/Data-Plane) on USER
+# edits — inotify + debounce, inside the Pulse process (Linux launchd-WatchPaths equivalent).
+# The daily `derived-sync` cron job stays as the safety-net for missed events.
+
 [hooks]
 enabled = true
 blocked_skills = ["keybindings-help"]
